<ptxt>Vacuum Switching Valve Assembly NO.1</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Resistance Inspection</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A128942J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1 - 2</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>20°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>23 to 26Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</s3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Operation Check</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Apply battery voltage between the terminals of the vacuum switching valve assembly No.1, and check for air flow between each port when the coil is energized and not energized.</ptxt>
<table>
<title>Standard:</title>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.06in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Energized Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Specified Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Energized</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Air flows</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Not energized</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>No air flow</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
